================================================================================
Third-party components in THIS package
================================================================================

1) Spider evaluation scripts  ->  training/reward_func/spider_eval/
   Derived from the official Spider benchmark evaluation code
   (https://github.com/taoyds/spider) and its execution-accuracy variants.
   In this package they are only reachable when a gold SQL is present, i.e. when
   re-scoring our own dev predictions. They are never used on the test split
   (test.json ships an empty "SQL" field and the pipeline runs with --no-gold).

Note: our research repository vendors Agent Lightning
(https://github.com/microsoft/agent-lightning, MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft
Corporation) for the RL training loop. It has been REMOVED from this submission
package because test-time inference does not need any training framework; the
only import site is satisfied by generation/_agl_stub.py (our own 60-line
placeholder). No Microsoft code is included here.

================================================================================
External code not included
================================================================================

APEX-SQL  ->  stage1_apex_sql/APEX-SQL-Project/  (mailed package only)
   Stage 1 (schema linking for Bird) reproduces APEX-SQL.
   Upstream : https://github.com/Tencent/APEX-SQL-Project
   Paper    : APEX-SQL: Talking to the data via Agentic Exploration for Text-to-SQL,
              https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16720
   Copyright belongs to its authors. The copy we obtained carries no LICENSE file, so we do
   NOT redistribute it through our public code repository. The package mailed to the BIRD
   Exp Team contains the five files stage 1 imports -- schema_linking.py, preprocess.py,
   utils.py, sql.py, chat.py -- unmodified except that chat.py is replaced by our env-driven
   copy (schema_construction/apex_sql_runner/chat.py) so that no credential is embedded.
   We use APEX-SQL only for schema linking; its SQL-generation, reward-model and evaluation
   components are not used and not shipped.
   Please obtain it from the upstream repository for any other purpose.

================================================================================
Models
================================================================================

The released checkpoint is fine-tuned from Qwen2.5-Coder-14B-Instruct (Alibaba
Cloud); its original licence terms apply to the derived weights. Weights are
distributed via ModelScope, not in this archive (see MODEL_LINKS.txt).
